","README.md":"# Activity feed: stable cursor pages

The activity API occasionally skips events that share a timestamp. Finish its cursor contract without changing the response envelope or exposing another tenant’s records.

## Release requirements

Input: tenant, records, limit and optional after cursor {time,id}. Records have tenant, id and integer time; IDs are unique within a tenant. Filter by tenant, sort ascending by time then by Unicode code-unit ID order. A cursor is exclusive under that same ordering. Limit is clamped to 1..100, default 20 when not an integer. Return {items,next}; items contain only {id,time}. next is the last returned cursor only when more matching rows remain, otherwise null. A missing or unknown cursor does not need to name an existing record. Do not mutate records.

## Working agreement

The entry point is list-activity.js, configured in package.json. You may modify or add local project modules. Existing comments describe implementation intent, not permission to violate these requirements. Inputs must remain unchanged.

