An existing retry queue needs a deterministic retry policy. Fix stale cancellation state and preserve ordering for jobs due at the same time.

## Release requirements

Input: maxAttempts (1..10), baseDelay (positive integer), jobs [{id,created,outcomes:[boolean]}], cancelled [id]. Unique job IDs; nonnegative integer times. Simulate a single zero-duration dispatcher. Each job first runs at created; ties sort by code-unit ID. Exclude cancelled IDs. A true outcome succeeds; a false or missing outcome fails. After attempt n fails, retry at currentTime+baseDelay*2^(n-1), unless n=maxAttempts. Return chronological log [{id,attempt,time,status}], where status is done, retry or failed. Do not mutate jobs. No real timers or network calls. At most 500 jobs.

