","README.md":"# Admission gateway: weighted quotas and retry identity

Ship weighted per-tenant admission control without penalizing rejected retries. Repair boundary and namespace bugs in the inherited gateway.

## Release requirements

Request data: limit is a nonnegative integer quota; window is a positive duration. requests arrive in nondecreasing integer time order. Each request identifies tenant and user, with time, cost and optional id. A reset request instead has reset=true.

Quota: count only accepted costs in the interval strictly after time-window and through time. Accept a positive integer cost only when the current sum plus cost is at most limit. Rejects consume no quota. Tenant/user identity is a pair, so delimiter-containing names cannot collide.

Retry identity: remember accepted request IDs separately for each tenant/user. The same ID, time and cost replays true without consuming quota. A changed payload returns false. Rejected IDs remain reusable; accepted IDs remain remembered after the quota window expires.

Reset: clear the current quota window for that tenant/user, preserve accepted ID history and return true. Other namespaces are unaffected. Return an ordered array of booleans. Arbitrary string IDs and exact expiry boundaries must be safe.

## Working agreement

The entry point is admit-request.js, configured in package.json. You may modify or add local project modules. Existing comments describe implementation intent, not permission to violate these requirements. Inputs must remain unchanged.

Run Examples exercises the public examples. Full Check runs the hidden workload and regression suite.
